    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.00155_p29_b1",
      "text": "RLHF is optimization under a misspecified reward: the policy is trained against a learned\n",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        104.46,
        523.33,
        116.29
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        288,
        417,
        2093,
        465
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 11.84,
      "font_name": "LMRoman12-Regular",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 89,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.00155_p29_b2",
      "text": "proxy, but deployment quality is judged by latent human preferences. The key modeling\nchoice is therefore where to place pessimism. We argue that regret is the right target.\nWorst-case value protects a policy in isolation; worst-case regret compares it with the\n",
      "bbox": [
        71.4,
        122.31,
        525.58,
        170.13
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        285,
        489,
        2102,
        680
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 11.93,
      "font_name": "LMRoman12-Regular",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 261,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.00155_p29_b3",
      "text": "hindsight-best policy under the same plausible reward, matching the loss induced by\nobjective misspecification more directly.\n",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        175.98,
        523.73,
        205.96
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        288,
        703,
        2094,
        823
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 12.07,
      "font_name": "LMRoman12-Regular",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 125,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.00155_p29_b4",
      "text": "Under norm-induced Wasserstein ambiguity, the promptwise RLHF problem admits a\ndual-norm closed-form adversary. In the \u21131 specialization, this structure further yields a\nwater-filling optimal policy and a coordinate-local bonus that can be translated into a\n",
      "bbox": [
        71.58,
        212.0,
        523.37,
        259.76
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        286,
        847,
        2093,
        1039
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 11.87,
      "font_name": "LMRoman12-Regular",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 257,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.00155_p29_b5",
      "text": "GRPO-compatible reward-shaping algorithm with light computational overhead. Empiri-\ncally, the resulting DRRO correction mitigates over-optimization more effectively than\n",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        265.76,
        525.29,
        295.62
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        288,
        1063,
        2101,
        1182
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 11.9,
      "font_name": "LMRoman12-Regular",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 170,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.00155_p29_b6",
      "text": "the tested baselines, while standard value-robust DRO is systematically over-pessimistic.\n",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        301.58,
        525.4,
        313.51
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
